[0.009462, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.009503, "o", "== The tests of S1 to S9 (Postgres, with the roles of Petra, the Platform object and the views)\r\n\r\n$ npm test -w @tensquads/costs 2>&1 | grep -E '^ *✔ S[0-9]+|^ℹ (tests|fail)'\r\n"]
[0.392077, "o", "✔ S1: the amount is the units times the price of one unit, in whole millionths, rounded half up (1.005256ms)\r\n"]
[0.392777, "o", "✔ S1: a model call of a gateway call gives two rows, one for input and one for output, with the attempt (1.781925ms)\r\n"]
[0.393347, "o", "✔ S1: a model call in a command has the key of the command, and the sandbox and a service have their keys (0.797627ms)\r\n"]
[0.393905, "o", "✔ S9: the budget of a task is reached when the sum of its cost rows is at the limit or above (0.796201ms)\r\n"]
[0.394397, "o", "✔ S4: an amount that does not divide evenly gives whole parts, the remainder by the account ids, and the sum is the amount (0.691212ms)\r\n"]
[0.394725, "o", "✔ S4: the parts follow the usage, and the remainder goes to the largest fractions first (0.228858ms)\r\n"]
[0.395143, "o", "✔ S4: with no usage, the parts are equal (0.161727ms)\r\n"]
[0.406833, "o", "ℹ tests 7\r\n"]
[0.407027, "o", "ℹ fail 0\r\n"]
[0.424711, "o", "[exit 0]\r\n"]
[0.425028, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.425125, "o", "$ cd apps/platform && npx tsx --test test/costs.test.ts test/shared-costs.test.ts test/views.test.ts 2>&1 | grep -E '^ *(✔|✖) S[0-9]+|^ℹ (tests|fail)'\r\n"]
[1.613155, "o", "✔ S1: the same gateway call two times gives one row; a turn that runs again in a new attempt gives two rows; the cost of the task is the sum of both (420.84173ms)\r\n"]
[1.85813, "o", "✔ S1: three step calls 400 ms apart give three sandbox rows of 400 ms each, and their amount is not 0 (245.119599ms)\r\n"]
[2.178997, "o", "✔ S1: the checker model, a decider in a command of Petra, an outside service and a model call of Petra each add their rows (321.459706ms)\r\n"]
[2.446544, "o", "✔ S2: a cost row keeps the price of its time, and a new price does not change an old row (268.485162ms)\r\n"]
[2.494137, "o", "✔ S3: costs and credits are in different tables, no table has a stored sum, and the admin schema has only views (45.618304ms)\r\n"]
[3.174119, "o", "✔ S9: a task stops with max_budget when its cost rows over two attempts reach the limit of its task type (681.647307ms)\r\n"]
[3.174405, "o", "✔ S1: a model call of Petra in her conversation has the key of the command of the newest owner message (0.595866ms)\r\n"]
[3.690894, "o", "✔ S4: an amount that does not divide evenly between three accounts gives whole parts, and their sum is the amount (197.6732ms)\r\n"]
[3.89779, "o", "✔ S4: the Platform object stops after the first share, one account gets a new cost row, and the second run keeps the parts (207.016926ms)\r\n"]
[4.02402, "o", "✔ S4: with no usage in the period, the parts are equal between the accounts that existed in it (125.930298ms)\r\n"]
[4.430841, "o", "✔ S5: a correction adds rows that cancel the old parts and rows for the new parts; no row changes; the view has the new amount (407.478861ms)\r\n"]
[5.244333, "o", "✔ S6: the views for each account, task type, bot, model and decision point give the expected numbers (457.970819ms)\r\n"]
[5.553034, "o", "✔ S7: the operations view gives stuck tasks, waiting approvals, check failures and cost rows with no price (310.576826ms)\r\n"]
[5.566406, "o", "✔ S6, S7: no view has a column with the text of a message, a brief, a fact or an action (11.435257ms)\r\n"]
[5.607348, "o", "✔ S8: the role of the views cannot read an account table, and the trail read writes admin_reads before it gives the rows (42.662726ms)\r\n"]
[5.620007, "o", "ℹ tests 15\r\nℹ fail 0\r\n"]
[5.645247, "o", "[exit 0]\r\n\r\n$ cd apps/platform && npx vitest run -c vitest.config.ts test-workers/admin.test.ts 2>&1 | grep -E 'S8|Tests '\r\n"]
[10.376634, "o", "      Tests  4 passed (4)\r\n"]
